// cwe_798_unfired.strata -- T-0145 per-CWE litmus, design-finding
// fixture: CWE-798 (Use of Hard-coded Credentials) is cataloged with
// `capability_kind=None` (`_threat.py::CWE_CATALOG`'s own comment:
// "secret-resting-at-low-clearance precondition, already the lattice's
// own clearance-violation refusal; no capability kind fires it"). No
// `may` atom can ever drag this obligation in -- same structural gap as
// CWE-22/CWE-352 (docs/strata/threat.md#the-litmus-coverage-
// cwe-22352798-never-fire-by-design). This fixture models a low-
// clearance node reachable from a foreign caller precisely to prove the
// negative: THREAT003 reports ZERO CWE-798 obligations here (the
// obligation this id names is refuted by the LATTICE's own
// clearance-violation machinery, a separate already-shipped mechanism,
// not THREAT003). No hardened twin: there is nothing to discharge when
// nothing fires.
//
// tested end to end (parse -> elaborate -> check_discharge_completeness)
// by tests/unit/strata/test_litmus_cwe.py, which asserts this NON-firing
// explicitly rather than skipping the id.

module cwe_798_unfired

node client : foreign { clearance Public; }
node secret_store : trusted {
    clearance Internal;
}

flow f_access : client -> secret_store { label Public; }
